Moon installs and enables moon-personal.service, a system service that runs
the daemon continuously under the unprivileged moon account. Its state is in
/var/lib/moon. This service is suitable for unattended operation, but desktop
notifications and desktop audio are only available to a logged-in user session.

For desktop notifications and audio, enable the per-user service after
installing the package:

  systemctl --user enable --now moon-personal-user.service

The user service uses the normal ~/.config/moon state and can be disabled with
systemctl --user disable --now moon-personal-user.service.